{
  "schema_version": "1.6.2",
  "id": "BIT-mlflow-2026-69146",
  "summary": "MLflow: LogInputs endpoint bypasses per-run UPDATE authorization in basic-auth",
  "details": "MLflow is an open source AI engineering platform for agents, large language models, and machine learning models. From 3.13.0 until 3.15.0, LogInputs is absent from BEFORE_REQUEST_HANDLERS in the mlflow/server/auth package, allowing any authenticated user to call POST /api/2.0/mlflow/runs/log-inputs for another user's run_id and inject attacker-controlled DatasetInput records into the dataset_inputs lineage metadata without UPDATE permission. This issue is fixed in version 3.15.0.",
